  "query_preview": "..FOR EXTREME SOUTHWESTERN CALIFORNIA INCLUDING ORANGE...\nSAN DIEGO...WESTERN RIVERSIDE AND SOUTHWESTERN SAN BERNARDINO\nCOUNTIES...\n\n\n...UPDATED AVIATION DISCUSSION...\n\nWidespread cloud coverage is being observed associated with \nmoisture from Tropical Cyclone Marie with showers expected to stop \nearly this evening. Lingering moisture tomorrow and Tuesday will \ncontinue chances of precipitation, mainly over the mountains. \nAfternoon shower and potentially thunderstorm chances will \ncontinue into Thursday. A ridge of high pressure will build from \nthe south for the middle of the week which will turn the upper \nlevel flow southeasterly. Currently Wednesday looks like the most \nlikely day for showers and thunderstorms to develop over the \nmountains in the afternoon. Low confidence in details surrounding \nrainfall rates at this time. Shower and thunderstorm chances have \ndecreased for Thursday, with the potential for the ridge of high \npressure moving right over Southern California, which would result\nin a very stable air mass aloft.\n\nHigh temperatures Monday are expected to be 5 to 10 degrees \nwarmer than today, with less cloud coverage expected. High \ntemperatures will continue to increase into Wednesday for areas \nwest of the mountains and Thursday for the deserts. Above average \nhigh and low temperatures can be expected for the majority of this\nweek. Widespread minor to moderate HeatRisk is expected for \ninland areas Tuesday through Thursday.",
